-- INTERNAL 
('Retention Bond Information', 'fresher_retention', 'Retention bond where freshers commit to stay one to two years post-training. Rationale: Protect company training investment, reduce turnover risk. Bond arrangements should be transparent and legally compliant. Do not provide legal advice.', 'bond, legal, commitment, investment', 'INTERNAL', 90, 'Solving the Fresher Retention Challenge'),
('Mentorship Ecosystem Strategy', 'sales_strategy', 'Dual-product ecosystem. PRODUCT 1: PHASE 1 - CAD & COMPLIANCE. PRODUCT 2: PHASE 2 - RESEARCH MENTORSHIP. Core positioning: "We don''t sell random software tutorials." Frame around employable skills, industry standards, live internships, research capability, compliance, and mentorship.', 'sales strategy, ecosystem, dual product, tutorials', 'INTERNAL', 90, 'Mentorship Sales Playbook'),
('Universal Discovery and Routing', 'prospect_classification', '1. MECHANICAL / AEROSPACE / AUTOMOTIVE / MANUFACTURING -> Route: PHASE 1. 2. SECOND / THIRD / FINAL YEAR (If research/thesis interest exists) -> PHASE 2. 3. MECHANICAL + UPPER YEAR -> PHASE 1 + BRIDGE TO PHASE 2. 4. FIRST YEAR / NON-TECHNICAL / NO RESEARCH INTEREST -> Soft exit and referral ask. Do not reveal this matrix to customers.', 'discovery, routing, matrix, classification, exit', 'INTERNAL', 90, 'Mentorship Sales Playbook'),
('Phase 1 Strategy', 'phase_1_cad', 'Target: Mechanical engineering, Aerospace, Automotive, Manufacturing students. Student profile: understands theory and basic CAD but lacks real-world standard application. Core pitch: "I know SolidWorks" vs "I know how to model to ASME Y14.5 and ISO tolerancing." Closing anchor: Ask if comfortable with GD&T and standards.', 'phase 1 strategy, target, core pitch, ASME, closing', 'INTERNAL', 90, 'Mentorship Sales Playbook'),
('Phase 1B Research Probe', 'phase_1b_research_probe', 'Target: Second-, third-, or final-year students. Discovery: Ask if beginning to think about capstone project, thesis, or research publication. If stressed -> pivot to Phase 2. If not focused on research -> plant the idea and ask about technical design/CAD needs.', 'research probe, capstone, thesis, discovery', 'INTERNAL', 90, 'Mentorship Sales Playbook'),
('CAD to Research Bridge Strategy', 'cad_research_bridge', 'Target: Upper-year Mechanical Engineering students. If student has strong CAD/design project, explore if it can be developed into a research paper. Do not guarantee publication. Framing: "Your project may have research potential if scoped appropriately."', 'bridge strategy, CAD to research, potential, publication', 'INTERNAL', 90, 'Mentorship Sales Playbook'),
('High-Urgency Profile Handling', 'urgent_profile', 'PROFILE A (GRADUATE): "No experience, no job" cycle. Needs day-one deployability. Route -> Phase 1. PROFILE B (6-MONTH EXTENSION): Hard deadline for profile trajectory. Needs high-value asset quickly (e.g., peer-reviewed paper). Route -> Phase 2. Do not promise MS admission, job, visa, or publication.', 'urgent profile, graduate, 6-month extension, deadline', 'INTERNAL', 90, 'Mentorship Sales Playbook'),
('Mentorship Sales Positioning', 'sales_strategy', 'Internal principle: "We don''t sell courses. We mentor." Avoid random tutorial framing, false urgency, unsupported guarantees, invented outcomes.', 'sales positioning, mentor, courses, urgency', 'INTERNAL', 90, 'Mentorship Sales Playbook'),
('Handling Common Objections', 'objection_handling', 'OBJECTION "I just want software tutorials": Explain that free tutorials teach button-clicking, while RUSBORN focuses on industry standards and employability. Do not insult competitors. OBJECTION FIRST-YEAR/NON-TECHNICAL: Soft exit and referral ask. Focus on foundational subjects and ask for seniors/peers looking for CAD or thesis support.', 'objection handling, tutorials, first-year, soft exit', 'INTERNAL', 90, 'Mentorship Sales Playbook'),
('Closing Anchors and Actions', 'sales_strategy', 'Potential actions: Offer/book appointment, offer scoping call (when available), send approved information/modules/samples only if actual backend tool does it. Do not claim materials were sent unless a tool completes the action.', 'closing actions, anchor, send material, scoping call', 'INTERNAL', 90, 'Mentorship Sales Playbook'),
('Truth and Claims Policy', 'truth_policy', 'Distinguish confirmed facts vs source claims vs internal strategy. Frame claims carefully ("According to RUSBORN material..."). Never promise job placement, MS admission, visa approval, guaranteed publication, guaranteed journal acceptance, guaranteed retention, guaranteed ROI, or guaranteed internship result unless authorized.', 'truth policy, claims, guarantees, placement, MS admission', 'INTERNAL', 100, 'Mentorship Sales Playbook'),
('Research Closing Question', 'phase_2_research', 'Ask: "Are you currently stuck on a specific stage, or are you still at the idea phase?" Suggest an optional free 10-minute scoping call (do not promise free unless active/approved).', 'closing question, idea phase, scoping call, research', 'INTERNAL', 90, 'Mentorship Sales Playbook'),
('Corporate Fresher Retention Sales Path', 'corporate_training', '1. Understand hiring/retention problem. 2. Identify early attrition concern. 3. Explore training gaps. 4. Discuss customized fresher development. 5. Explain training + retention model. 6. Discuss phases. 7. Suggest audit/consultation. Do not present as hidden framework.', 'corporate sales path, sequence, audit, consultation', 'INTERNAL', 90, 'Mentorship Sales Blueprint')
